{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>וַיִּבְרָא אֱלֹהִים אֶת הָאָדָם בְּצַלְמוֹ</b>. The meaning of בְּצַלְמוֹ is the form recognizable in man, and the intention is that He created his golem (unformed body) and also his form. And afterward it says <b>בְּצֶלֶם אֱלֹהִים</b> — by this He made known to us the form in which He created him, namely that it is the form of Elohim." "It further intends to say that He created man in two forms: the first is the form recognizable in every man, even in the sons of man who are empty of holiness, who are not of Israel — and concerning them it says <b>בְּצַלְמוֹ</b>, meaning the form of the created being. And the second is the aspect of those endowed with fortune, the nation of Israel, the inheritance of Shaddai — concerning them it says <b>בְּצֶלֶם אֱלֹהִים</b> He created him. This comes to teach us that there are in created beings two forms: the recognizable form, and the form of Elohim — a spiritual, concealed form. Understand:"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T18:57:23.843139332Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}